Complete DSA Roadmap for Basic to Advanced/Pro
Phase 1: Foundation Building (Basics)
Goal: Build a strong base in core concepts.

!. Understand Big-O Notation

* Time Complexity

* Space Complexity

* Common Complexities (O(1), O(n), O(log n), O(n²))

2. Master Basic Data Structures

* Arrays

* Strings

* Linked Lists (Singly, Doubly)

* Stacks

* Queues

3.  Start Simple Problem Solving
Solve basic problems for each topic (5-10 problems/topic)

Phase 2: Intermediate Data Structures and Recursion
Goal: Get confident in applying basic concepts.

1.  Learn Recursion

* Base case, Recursive calls

* Tail recursion

* Basic recursion problems (Factorial, Fibonacci, etc.)

2. Learn Searching and Sorting

* Linear Search, Binary Search

* Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, Insertion Sort

* Merge Sort, Quick Sort

3.  Important Intermediate Data Structures

* HashMaps and HashSets

* Priority Queues (Heaps)

* Two Pointers Technique

* Sliding Window Technique

4. Solve Medium-level Problems
(about 10-20 problems each on recursion, searching, sorting, hashmaps)

Phase 3: Advanced Data Structures
Goal: Handle complex real-world problems.

1.  Trees

* Binary Trees

* Binary Search Trees (BST)

* Tree Traversals (Inorder, Preorder, Postorder)

Problems: Height of tree, Diameter, Symmetric tree, etc.

2.  Graphs

* Representation (Adjacency list, matrix)

* DFS, BFS

* Shortest Path Algorithms (Dijkstra, Floyd-Warshall)

* Topological Sort

* Minimum Spanning Tree (Kruskal, Prim)

3. Dynamic Programming (DP)

* Understand Memoization, Tabulation

* Famous Problems:

* 0/1 Knapsack

* Longest Common Subsequence

* Coin Change Problem

* Matrix Chain Multiplication

4. Greedy Algorithms

* Activity Selection

* Fractional Knapsack

* Huffman Coding

5. Backtracking

* N-Queens Problem

* Sudoku Solver

* Rat in Maze

Phase 4: Problem-Solving Practice (Pro Level)
Goal: Build speed, accuracy, and deep thinking.

1. Competitive Coding Platforms

LeetCode (TOP)

Codeforces / CodeChef (for speed)

GeeksForGeeks (for concepts)

2. Set Targets

100 Easy Problems

150 Medium Problems

50 Hard Problems

3. Focus Topics for Advanced Problems

Segment Trees

Trie (Prefix Tree)

Disjoint Set Union (DSU)

Bit Manipulation Tricks

String Algorithms (KMP, Rabin Karp)

4. Contests and Time-Bound Practice

Participate in Weekly LeetCode Contests.

Simulate coding rounds:
Set 90 mins → Solve 3 medium + 1 hard problem.

